WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.910
Among the many shocking developments in Avengers:
Endgame, Thor's transformation from buff God

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.920
of Thunder to depressed dad bod has to rank
near the top of the list and while there's

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.540
a lot to love about this narrative twist,
it's far from perfect.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.860
Here are the three best and worst things about
Thick Thor.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.800
Heroes always have their low points, but Thor's
is pretty darn low.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.490
He spends the bulk of Infinity War off on
his own side quest in the hopes of coming

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.860
back with a weapon that could ultimately turn
the tide and it almost does, too.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.820
When we get to Endgame, though, Thor isn't
just distracted by his own motivations and

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.760
plans, he's completely lost his way.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.940
Throughout much of Endgame, "Bro Thor," as
Marvel officially labels him in a Blu-ray

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.480
featurette, continually makes poor decisions
and prioritizes his own needs over everyone

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:40.980
else's.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.760
This is immediately made clear when Rocket
and Professor Hulk arrive in New Asgard to

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.790
find that the "king" is hiding away playing
video games and only interacts with his people

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.170
in order to restock on beer.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:53.970
And what about when he time travels to Asgard
with Rocket in order to extract the Aether

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.620
from his old flame, Jane Foster?

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.290
He crumbles in fear as soon as the rubber
hits the road, needing Rocket's tough-guy

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.100
pep talk to help him turn a corner.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.380
Which even then, doesn’t work!

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.780
"I think I'm having a panic attack."

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:04.860
"Get it together!"

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:09.700
By the time Avengers and Thor: The Dark World
rolled around, the one-dimensional aspect

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.900
of Thor's character as a musclebound hero
was getting old fast.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.320
The early manifestations of the son of Odin
were powerful and all, but there just wasn't

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.560
much substance there … that is, until director
Taika Waititi arrived on the scene.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:25.400
Thor: Ragnarok reinvigorated the Thor franchise
with a humorous energy that thrilled audiences

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.260
across the board.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:30.700
The threequel strips down Thor's story to
its emotionally raw underpinnings and provides

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.409
the perfect springboard to carry the character
through his vengeful mission in Avengers:

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:35.020
Infinity War.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:39.780
In Endgame, the "Bro Thor" narrative twists
the story even further, dragging the Asgardian

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.030
to all new lows before ultimately bringing
him some long-awaited emotional resolution.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:48.020
The developments in Thor's story from Ragnarok
through Endgame didn't seem possible in the

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.560
early days of the second phase of the MCU,
and the entire affair stands as a testament

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.920
to the inherent potential that the character
possesses.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.780
For all of his heroics and character development
over the years, Thor really is still a gruff

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:00.860
warrior at his core.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:05.060
That's why he went off in search of a bigger,
badder weapon when Thanos arrived on the scene.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:08.649
If he could outgun his opponent, he knew he
could win by sheer brute force.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:12.490
But, while his strong-handed approach to life
has been instrumental on multiple Earth- and

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:17.560
universe-saving occasions, there's one moment
in Endgame that exposes how nasty Thor's belligerent,

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.880
competitive attitude can get when he's off
duty.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.910
When Rocket and Hulk arrive at Thor's hut,
the trio of heroes catch up on the past five

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.950
years and discuss future plans while Korg
plays Fortnite off to the side.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:33.011
At one point, Korg informs Thor that "NoobMaster69"
is giving him a hard time again, at which

00:02:33.011 --> 00:02:37.069
point the God of Thunder grabs his friend's
headset and delivers a thundering string of

00:02:37.069 --> 00:02:40.880
threats, including literally flying to the
person's house and tearing off his arms.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.740
The little spurt of cyberbullying exposes
the fact that, while Thor's brazen approach

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:49.239
to life may work out well in the hero department,
when it comes to the regular, everyday stuff

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.040
he sometimes ends up looking like a bully.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.160
Thor is an alien.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.260
He can fly around the universe using the Bifrost.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.980
The guy survived floating through space until
the Guardians of the Galaxy picked him up

00:02:58.980 --> 00:02:59.760
in Infinity War.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:03.850
And yet, over the years he's become one of
the most oddly relatable characters in the

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.440
MCU.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:08.460
In spite of the rather exaggerated nature
of everything he does, the truth is, Thor

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:12.910
has had some very human struggles over the
years, a fact that is on full display during

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:13.400
Endgame.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.280
He'd suffered heartbreak and emotional trauma
more than once leading up to the film, but

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.989
it's in Endgame that we come face to face
with a Thor that is truly relatable.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:25.260
As he grapples with his emotions, struggles
through depression, and faces the consequences

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.800
for his actions, it becomes easier than ever
to connect with the god on entirely new levels.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.830
On a more practical note, his hefty appearance
also creates new frontiers.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:37.069
Thor's bod opens up a whole new world for
cosplayers to connect with their favorite

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:39.330
Avenger without feeling inadequate in the
process.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.180
While the Son of Odin is a heavy hitter whether
he's sporting a beer gut or not, when you

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:48.300
break it down, all the extra weight and years
of inactivity in Endgame do seem to take their

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.360
toll on the Asgardian's ability to keep up.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:51.080
"Thor!"

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.420
"Is he asleep?"

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.940
Thor is definitely slower this time around.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:59.069
In fact, Hemsworth filmed scenes with weights
on his hands and ankles to change the appearance

00:03:59.069 --> 00:03:59.680
of his walk.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:03.920
He also doesn't make quite as big of a splash
in the final battle as he did, say, when he

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.610
arrived in Wakanda in Infinity War.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:09.620
In fact, this time around he finds himself
so outmatched by Thanos that he ultimately

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.520
needs to be bailed out by the Mjolnir -wielding
Steve Rogers.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:13.280
"Give me that.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:14.220
You have the little one."

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:18.120
Of course, it's natural that he'd be a bit
rusty after taking five years off and packing

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:19.130
on so many pounds.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.900
There's no question that the effects of his
new lifestyle ultimately ended up hampering

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:27.240
his battlefield prowess a bit, which is an
unfortunate turn for fans of Thor's epic approach

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:27.840
to combat.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:32.340
For all of the ups and downs the "Bro Thor"
character goes through in Endgame, hands down

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:36.300
one of the best things about the entire film
is his final decision to join the Guardians

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.080
of the Galaxy.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.410
While his presence will be missed on the Avengers,
the thought of an overweight, self-confident

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:45.570
Thor, unhampered by responsibilities, traipsing
around the cosmos with the Guardians in search

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.820
of adventure is the definition of awesome.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.430
The thought that the entire scenario will
be overseen in Guardians 3 by the offbeat

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:54.600
genius of director James Gunn makes it that
much more appealing.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.699
From adding some muscle to the already impressive
team, to his ongoing bickering with Star-Lord

00:04:58.699 --> 00:05:01.010
over who's really in charge, the possibilities
are tantalizing.

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:05.430
We'll have to wait and see if the "Asgardians
of the Galaxy" really will be a full-length

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:09.830
feature affair or if it'll just be a passing
nod as Thor heads into the unknown for a fourth

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:10.580
solo film.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.080
Then again, maybe we'll get both.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.000
Here's hoping.

